@page "/components/ai/thinkingindicator"
@inherits AppComponentBase

<PageOutlet Url="components/ai/thinkingindicator"
            Title="AiThinkingIndicator"
            Description="BitAiThinkingIndicator shows that an AI model is working on a reply that has not started yet: bouncing dots and a label, announced politely to screen readers." />

<DemoPage Name="AiThinkingIndicator"
          SecondaryNames="@(["TypingIndicator"])"
          Description="BitAiThinkingIndicator is shown while the model is working but has produced nothing yet: three bouncing dots and a label, drawn at the size of the text around it. It is a polite live region, so a screen reader user learns that a response is coming without the announcement interrupting them. The label says Thinking by default, or whatever the app knows about the wait - a tool that is running, a status the transport reported."
          Parameters="componentParameters"
          SubClasses="componentSubClasses"
          CssVariables="componentCssVariables"
          GitHubAIUrl="ThinkingIndicator/BitAiThinkingIndicator.razor"
          GitHubDemoUrl="AI/ThinkingIndicator/BitAiThinkingIndicatorDemo.razor">
    <NotesTemplate>
        <BitText>
            To use this component, you need to install the
            <BitLink Href="https://www.nuget.org/packages/Bit.BlazorUI.AI" Target="_blank">
                <BitTag Reversed
                        Text="Bit.BlazorUI.AI"
                        Color="BitColor.SecondaryBackground"
                        IconName="@BitIconName.NavigateExternalInline" />
            </BitLink>
            nuget package, as described in the Optional steps of the
            <BitLink Href="/getting-started">Getting started</BitLink> page.
        </BitText>
        <br />
        <BitText>
            A chat message shows one by itself while its reply has not started. The indicator is a polite live region
            (<b>role="status"</b>): render it only while there is a wait to announce, and change its <b>Label</b> rather than rendering a new
            one, so a screen reader hears each status once. Under reduced motion the dots slow down rather than stop, since they are the only
            sign that work is still going on; ForceAnimation at the top of this page restores their pace. See the <BitLink Href="/ai/scenarios/streaming">Streaming</BitLink> and
            <BitLink Href="/ai/scenarios/tools">Tools</BitLink> scenarios.
        </BitText>
    </NotesTemplate>
    <Examples>
        <DemoExample Title="Basic" RazorCode="@example1RazorCode" Id="example1">
            <div>
                Three dots and the <b>Thinking</b> label of the <b>BitAiStrings</b> in force, drawn inline at the size of the text around it.
            </div>
            <br />
            <BitAiThinkingIndicator />
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Label" RazorCode="@example2RazorCode" Id="example2">
            <div>
                <b>Label</b> replaces the default text with what the app knows about the wait. It is what the live region announces.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div class="example-stack">
                <BitAiThinkingIndicator Label="Searching the documentation" />
                <BitAiThinkingIndicator Label="Reading 3 attachments" />
                <BitAiThinkingIndicator Label="Waiting for the weather service" />
            </div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="While a reply is on its way" RazorCode="@example3RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example3CsharpCode" Id="example3">
            <div>
                Shown from the moment a turn starts until its first text arrives. The scripted model below first reports a status
                (<b>BitAiStatusEvent</b>, kept as the <b>StatusText</b> of the message) and then calls a tool, and the label follows both; once
                the answer starts streaming, the indicator gives way to it.
            </div>
            <br />
            <BitButton OnClick="AskAsync" Disabled="session.IsGenerating">Ask about the weather</BitButton>
            <br /><br />
            <div class="example-reply">
                @if (session.Conversation.Messages.LastOrDefault(m => m.Role.IsAssistant) is { } reply)
                {
                    @if (reply.PartsOf<BitAiTextPart>().Any(p => p.IsEmpty is false))
                    {
                        <div>@reply.GetText()</div>
                    }
                    else if (session.IsGenerating)
                    {
                        <BitAiThinkingIndicator Label="@WaitLabel(reply)" />
                    }
                }
            </div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Disabled" RazorCode="@example4RazorCode" Id="example4">
            <div>
                A <b>Disabled</b> indicator is drawn dimmed, its dots held still at the frame they had reached - for a wait the app has
                paused. It is still the live region that announces its label.
            </div>
            <br />
            <BitAiThinkingIndicator Disabled Label="Paused until you reconnect" />
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Cascading parameters" RazorCode="@example5RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example5CsharpCode" Id="example5">
            <div>
                <b>BitParams</b> with a <b>BitAiThinkingIndicatorParams</b> sets the look of every indicator inside it - the ones a chat
                message renders included - and an indicator's own value still wins (the last one brings its own <b>Styles</b>). The
                <b>Label</b> is never cascaded: it says what one wait is about.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div class="example-stack">
                <BitParams Parameters="thinkingParams">
                    <BitAiThinkingIndicator />
                    <BitAiThinkingIndicator Label="Searching the documentation" />
                    <BitAiThinkingIndicator Label="Reading 3 attachments" Styles="@(new() { Loading = new() { Label = "font-weight: bold" } })" />
                </BitParams>
            </div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="Style & Class" RazorCode="@example6RazorCode" Id="example6">
            <div>
                <b>Style</b> and <b>Class</b> land on the root, <b>Styles.Loading</b> and <b>Classes.Loading</b> on the parts of the
                <b>BitBouncingDotsLoading</b> it draws (its dots and its label). The public <b>--bit-AiThinkingIndicator-*</b> variables set the
                color and the size of the label - the dots are drawn at that size - and the <b>--bit-Loading-*</b> ones the dots themselves.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div class="example-stack">
                <BitAiThinkingIndicator Style="padding: 0.5rem 1rem; border-radius: 1rem; background-color: var(--bit-clr-pri-tint)" />

                <BitAiThinkingIndicator Class="custom-thinking" />

                <BitAiThinkingIndicator Styles="@(new() { Loading = new() { Label = "font-style: italic", Child = "background-color: #db2777" } })" />

                <BitAiThinkingIndicator Classes="@(new() { Root = "custom-thinking-root", Loading = new() { Label = "custom-thinking-label" } })" />

                <div style="--bit-AiThinkingIndicator-color: #0b7a75; --bit-AiThinkingIndicator-font-size: 1.25rem; --bit-Loading-color: #0b7a75;">
                    <BitAiThinkingIndicator />
                </div>
            </div>
        </DemoExample>

        <DemoExample Title="RTL" RazorCode="@example7RazorCode" CsharpCode="@example7CsharpCode" Id="example7">
            <div>
                In right-to-left text the dots lead from the right and the label follows them - whether the direction comes from
                <b>Dir</b> or from a <b>dir</b> attribute around the indicator. The default label is the <b>Thinking</b> text of the
                <b>BitAiStrings</b> in force - here a subclass of them, cascaded by a <b>BitAiOptionsProvider</b>.
            </div>
            <br />
            <div class="example-stack">
                <BitAiThinkingIndicator Dir="BitDir.Rtl" Label="در حال جستجوی مستندات" />
                <BitAiOptionsProvider UiOptions="persianOptions">
                    <div dir="rtl">
                        <BitAiThinkingIndicator />
                    </div>
                </BitAiOptionsProvider>
            </div>
        </DemoExample>
    </Examples>
</DemoPage>
